course: dictionary
lesson: 14854
title: Rappers and rhythm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rapper is a person who performs rap music. Rappers speak their words in rhythm, which means they follow a steady beat, and they often add rhymes, where words end with the same sound.
explain: «The rapper spoke fast, and every line rhymed with the beat.» The clues are beat and rhymed. A rapper speaks the words rather than singing them, and the words fit the rhythm of the music.
explain: Use the context to check your meaning. If the sentence is about songs, beats and rhymes, then rapper must be about music. Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A rapper is a person who performs rap music.
fact: Rap music means speaking words in rhythm and rhyme over a beat.
fact: «Rapper» is a noun, and its plural is «rappers».
fact: Rap began in New York among Black and Latino communities and spread around the world.
fact: Rare meaning: a rapper can also be something used for knocking, like a door knocker.
fact: Some rap songs have swearing or adult themes, so many have a «clean» version.
exercise: «The rapper's rhymes made the whole class clap along.» What is a rapper? | *A person who performs rap music, speaking in rhythm and rhyme | A person who paints pictures of animals | A person who sings opera on a stage | A person who sells newspapers
exercise: What do rappers do? | Count money in a bank | Paint pictures on walls | *Speak words in rhythm and rhyme over a beat | Swim fast in a pool
exercise: Copy the word from «My favourite rapper makes songs about friendship.» that names the person who performs. | songs | *rapper | friendship | favourite
test: «Before the visitors came in, they knocked with the brass rapper on the door.» What does rapper mean here? | A person who performs rap music | *Something used for knocking, like a door knocker | A loud bell in a church | A person who paints doors
test: «The radio played the clean version of the song, with no swear words.» What does clean suggest? | *The song has no swearing or adult themes | The song is wet and muddy | The song is the longest one ever | The song has no beat at all
exam: What is the plural of rapper? | rapperies | rapper's | rapping | *rappers
